(At its theoretical core, a computer is a physical realization of a Universal Turing Machine \(UTM\)—a mathematical model of computation) Tj
T* (formulated by Alan Turing in 1936. A Turing Machine consists of an infinite memory tape divided into cells, a read/write head, a state) Tj
T* (register, and a finite transition table. The Church-Turing Thesis postulates that any function computable by an effective algorithm can be) Tj
T* (computed by a Universal Turing Machine.) Tj
