(Published by John von Neumann in 1945 \("First Draft of a Report on the EDVAC"\), the stored-program architecture unified computer) Tj
T* (programs and computational data within the same shared addressable physical memory space. In contrast, the Harvard Architecture) Tj
T* (separates physical instruction memory \(read-only or modified by flash\) from physical data memory, providing dual simultaneous memory) Tj
T* (access channels at the cost of circuit complexity.) Tj
