(• 1st Generation \(1940-1956\): Vacuum Tubes. Massive room-sized machines \(ENIAC, UNIVAC I, EDVAC\), consuming kilowatts of power, relying) Tj
T* (on magnetic drum memory, programmed purely in binary machine code.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
39.6850393700787407 470.5514173228345953 Td
(• 2nd Generation \(1956-1963\): Transistors. Invention of the bipolar junction transistor at Bell Labs \(Shockley, Bardeen, Brattain\) replaced fragile) Tj
T* (vacuum tubes, enabling magnetic core memory, FORTRAN, COBOL, and assembly languages.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
