(CPL \(Combined Programming Language, initially named Cambridge Programming Language\) was a multi-institutional, ambitious systems) Tj
T* (and academic programming language developed jointly in 1962–1963 by the University of Cambridge Mathematical Laboratory \(led by) Tj
T* (Christopher Strachey and David Barron\) and the University of London Computer Unit. Developed specifically for the Titan Computer \(an) Tj
T* (experimental Atlas 2 computer\) at Cambridge and the Ferranti Atlas at London, CPL was conceived to bridge theoretical computer) Tj
T* (science with bare-metal operating system construction.) Tj
ET
