(In 1969 at Bell Telephone Laboratories, Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie began developing the UNIX operating system on a discarded) Tj
T* (Digital Equipment Corporation \(DEC\) PDP-7 minicomputer equipped with only 8 Kilobytes of core memory. Thompson wanted a high-level) Tj
T* (programming language to replace assembly, but BCPL was still too large to run comfortably in 8KB.) Tj
