(THE PDP-7 TO PDP-11 TRANSITION THAT BIRTHED C) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
62.3622047244094517 610.5829133858267141 Td
(PDP-7 \(Word-addressed 18-bit machine\) -> B Language fit perfectly.) Tj
T* (PDP-11 \(Byte-addressed 16-bit machine with 8-bit bytes\) -> B language could not efficiently index individual character bytes) Tj
T* (without manual pointer shifting. Dennis Ritchie recognized that hardware had evolved from word-oriented mainframes to) Tj
T* (byte-oriented minicomputers, requiring a language with explicit data types \(char, int\).) Tj
ET
