(Invariant: If the target value exists in the sorted array A, it must be located within the subarray A[low ... high].) Tj
T* (1. Initialization: Prior to loop, low = 0, high = n - 1. The target is guaranteed in A[0 ... n-1] if present.) Tj
T* (2. Maintenance: In each iteration, mid = \(low + high\) / 2. If A[mid] < target, target must be in right half \(low = mid + 1\). If A[mid]) Tj
T* (> target, target must be in left half \(high = mid - 1\). The invariant is preserved.) Tj
T* (3. Termination: Loop terminates when low > high \(element does not exist\) or A[mid] == target \(element found\). Correctness is) Tj
T* (proven!) Tj
