(• 2. Pure Interpreters: An interpreter reads source code line-by-line or token-by-token, parsing and executing actions on the fly without producing a) Tj
T* (persistent binary \(e.g., traditional Ruby, Bash, early Python\). Highly portable and flexible for interactive debugging, but significantly slower due to) Tj
T* (continuous instruction parsing.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
39.6850393700787407 461.4805511811022711 Td
(• 3. Hybrid Bytecode & JIT \(Just-In-Time\) Virtual Machines: Source code is pre-compiled into portable intermediate bytecode \(Java JVM bytecode) Tj
T* (or .NET CIL\). At runtime, the Virtual Machine interprets bytecode initially, while the JIT engine \(e.g., Java HotSpot, V8 TurboFan\) profiles) Tj
T* (execution, identifies "hot spots" \(frequently executed loops\), and compiles those methods directly into optimized native machine code in memory) Tj
T* (during execution!) Tj
