(• 1. Manual Memory Management \(C/C++\): Developers explicitly request memory using `malloc`/`free` or `new`/`delete`. Provides absolute control) Tj
T* (and zero latency spikes, but introduces severe software risks: memory leaks, dangling pointers, double-free vulnerabilities, and buffer overflows.) Tj
