(1. Parameters: a = 3, b = 4, f\(n\) = n*log\(n\).) Tj
T* (␀2␀.␀ ␀C␀r␀i␀t␀i␀c␀a␀l␀ ␀e␀x␀p␀o␀n␀e␀n␀t␀:␀ ␀l␀o␀g␀_␀b␀\(␀a␀\)␀ ␀=␀ ␀l␀o␀g␀_␀4␀\(␀3␀\)␀ "H␀ ␀0␀.␀7␀9␀2␀5␀.) Tj
T* (␀3␀.␀ ␀C␀o␀m␀p␀a␀r␀e␀ ␀f␀\(␀n␀\)␀ ␀t␀o␀ ␀n␀^␀\(␀l␀o␀g␀_␀b␀\(␀a␀\)␀\)␀:␀ ␀S␀i␀n␀c␀e␀ ␀f␀\(␀n␀\)␀ ␀=␀ ␀n␀*␀l␀o␀g␀\(␀n␀\)␀ ␀=␀ ©␀\(␀n␀^␀\(␀0␀.␀7␀9␀2␀5␀ ␀+␀ µ␀\)␀\)␀ ␀f␀o␀r␀ µ␀ "H␀ ␀0␀.␀2␀,␀ ␀t␀h␀i␀s␀ ␀i␀s␀ ␀c␀a␀n␀d␀i␀d␀a␀t␀e␀ ␀C␀a␀s␀e␀ ␀3␀.) Tj
T* (4. Regularity Condition Check: We must prove that a * f\(n/b\) <= c * f\(n\) for some constant c < 1 and sufficiently large n.) Tj
T* (   3 * f\(n/4\) = 3 * \(n/4\) * log\(n/4\) = \(3/4\) * n * \(log\(n\) - log\(4\)\) <= \(3/4\) * n * log\(n\).) Tj
T* (   Choosing c = 3/4 < 1 satisfies the condition for all n >= 4.) Tj
