(1. Cases:) Tj
T* (   - L1 TLB Hit \(95%\): EMAT_1 = L1_time + Memory_data = 0.5 + 50 = 50.5 ns.) Tj
T* (   - L2 TLB Hit \(4%\): EMAT_2 = L1_time + L2_time + Memory_data = 0.5 + 2.0 + 50 = 52.5 ns.) Tj
T* (   - TLB Miss \(1%\): Must traverse 4 levels of page tables in RAM + final data fetch = L1 + L2 + 4 * Memory + Memory_data =) Tj
T* (0.5 + 2.0 + 4 * 50 + 50 = 252.5 ns.) Tj
T* (2. Total EMAT = 0.95 * 50.5 + 0.04 * 52.5 + 0.01 * 252.5 = 47.975 + 2.100 + 2.525 = 52.60 ns.) Tj
T* (3. Impact of Huge Pages \(2MB / 1GB\): Increases TLB reach by orders of magnitude \(a single TLB entry covers 2MB instead) Tj
T* (of 4KB\), reducing TLB miss rate in memory-intensive databases from ~1% to <0.01%, virtually eliminating the 252.5 ns) Tj
T* (penalty.) Tj
