62.3622047244094517 568.346692913385823 Td
(1. Public parameters: p = 23, g = 5.) Tj
T* (2. Alice computes public key A = g^a mod p = 5^6 mod 23 = 15625 mod 23 = 8. Alice sends A = 8 to Bob.) Tj
T* (3. Bob computes public key B = g^b mod p = 5^15 mod 23 = 19. Bob sends B = 19 to Alice.) Tj
T* (4. Shared Secret Computation:) Tj
T* (   - Alice computes s = B^a mod p = 19^6 mod 23 = 47,045,881 mod 23 = 2.) Tj
T* (   - Bob computes s = A^b mod p = 8^15 mod 23 = 2.) Tj
T* (   Both independently arrive at shared symmetric key s = 2.) Tj
T* (5. Cryptographic Hardness: Security relies on the computational hardness of the Discrete Logarithm Problem \(DLP\) in finite) Tj
T* (cyclic groups: given g, p, and g^a mod p, it is computationally infeasible to find a when p is a large 2048+ bit prime.) Tj
