(1. Raft Node Roles: Follower, Candidate, Leader. Terms act as logical clocks.) Tj
T* (2. Quorum Requirement: To be elected Leader or commit a log entry, a node MUST receive positive votes / acknowledgments) Tj
T* (from a strict majority \(Quorum = floor\(N/2\) + 1\). For N=5, Quorum is 3.) Tj
T* (3. Partition Analysis:) Tj
T* (   - Partition with 2 nodes: Candidates cannot gather 3 votes; cannot elect a leader or commit writes.) Tj
T* (   - Partition with 3 nodes: Forms a valid Quorum \(3/5\). Can elect a leader and commit log entries.) Tj
T* (4. Split-Brain Impossibility: Because any two majorities of size floor\(N/2\)+1 must overlap in at least one node, it is) Tj
T* (mathematically impossible for two distinct leaders to obtain Quorum simultaneously. When partition heals, nodes with lower) Tj
T* (term update to the higher term leader and truncate uncommitted conflicting entries.) Tj
