(1. Token Bucket: Central Redis hash stores {last_refreshed_timestamp, current_tokens}. On request, tokens are replenished) Tj
T* (based on elapsed time * refill_rate. If tokens >= 1, decrement and allow; else reject \(HTTP 429\). Executed atomically via) Tj
T* (Redis Lua script to prevent race conditions. Memory overhead is minimal \(O\(1\) per user\).) Tj
T* (2. Sliding Window Log: Stores timestamps of requests in a Redis Sorted Set \(ZSET\). Removes timestamps older than) Tj
T* (current_time - 60s using ZREMRANGEBYSCORE. Card = ZCARD. If Card < limit, ZADD current_time and allow. Highly) Tj
T* (accurate, but high memory overhead \(O\(N\) where N is requests in window\).) Tj
T* (3. Production Architecture: Use Sliding Window Counter \(combines low memory of fixed window with accuracy of sliding) Tj
T* (window\) in Redis cluster with local in-memory token cache on API Gateways to reduce Redis network hops.) Tj
