(1. Clarification & Edge Cases: Explicitly ask about null inputs, array bounds, negative numbers, integer overflow, and) Tj
T* (duplicates.) Tj
T* (2. State Brute Force Upfront: Articulate naive solution with its Big-O time and space before writing any code.) Tj
T* (3. Pattern Recognition: Categorize into known patterns \(Sliding Window, Two Pointers, Monotonic Stack, Topological Sort, DP,) Tj
T* (Union-Find\).) Tj
T* (4. Step-by-Step Pseudocode: Walk through the algorithmic logic with the interviewer before writing code.) Tj
T* (5. Manual Dry-Run: Test the implementation line-by-line with a realistic test case, checking loop boundaries and termination.) Tj
